 "text_source": "captions_plus_linked_text",
 "notes": "Two branches from salting out: (1) protein concentration -> particle size (ends at conclusion; no loading/release test by size in packet); (2) pH -> secondary structure (and charge via MEC s10) -> zeta -> charge-driven loading -> release, which meets drug-charge ranking at the PRF. Table 1 (FSD fractions) and the chemical-stability claim for silk I particles (F5 linked text) are not in the packet and were left out. F4 and F7 have no panels offered: cited with panel_ids [] and figs. The F1b efficiency-vs-pH plot was not cited (crop cue class micrograph from the insets). Audit a1: RhB efficiency never near 100%, bounding s12. o12 rules out surface charge as the cause of the pH 7-9 release differences (zeta nearly flat from pH 7).",
